{
  "source": "SYNTHESISED from the real recording 04eff5c5-docs-only (pipeline 2859138213): one job, `verify:web_coverage_full 1/4`, added to the parent's job list with status `failed`, and the pipeline rows changed to failed to match. The name is the one the shipped example maps to `gate`; the shards really do run on the weekly schedule. No other field altered.",
  "note": "`gate` says a job is expected to sit UNRUN. The shipped example applies it to `re:^verify:web_coverage_full`, which is manual on main and automatic on the weekly schedule — so an override that also swallowed a job that RAN AND FAILED listed a red coverage shard under `gates`, where it could never red the icon. This project has no bridges on a docs-only push, so the tray sat on the outline check with exit 0.",
